was strip off all their clothing/armor.  The belief being that if
you weren't protected, you couldn't be hurt.  That would give it 
a real downside.  Best to implement this only if the enemy is at
a distance.

  The partial loss of control could be like being stunned, with a
certain possibility of moving/attacking toward the nearest 
monster, whether tame, peaceful, or hostile.

  Should be like being confused in that spells cannot be cast,
except for fireball, which does double damage.


  Tie in racial enmities.  Elves have a chance of going berserk 
when fighting orcs, and vice-versa, etc. 


  Let tame/peaceful/hostile monsters also have a chance of going 
berserk against their racial foes, including the player.

  When the berserk rage wears off, have the player sleep for 
awhile.  Just use the amulet of restful sleep code for that.

  Not sure it adds that much to Nethack.  Seems like it would 
work better in a pure hack&slash game (i.e. no magic).

